We shall study  $1$D stochastic Ginzburg-Landau equation on $\T$ as the following
\begin{equation} \label{e:XEqn}
\begin{cases}
\dif X_t + A X_t\dif t= N(X_t) \dif t + \dif L_t, \\
X_0=x,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] the nonlinear term $N$ is defined by
\begin{equation*} \label{e:NonlinearB}
N(u)= u-u^3 , \ \ \ \ \ u \in H.
\end{equation*}
